      ":question/worked-solution": "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nWe need\n\n$$\nf(c) = - c^{2} + c + 2=0.\n$$\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=-4 + 2 + 2 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=0 + 0 + 2 \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) &=-4 - 2 + 2 \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=2$.",
